On `v0.10.4`, the `resolved` on line [1122](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/18520ad6bbf7e6408b8449658326dc0c947c3507/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1122) is:

```lua
{
  error = {
    code = -32601,
    message = "Unhandled method completionItem/resolve",
    <metatable> = {
      __tostring = <function 1>
    }
  }
}

```

On nightly, that same resolved is:

```lua
{
  err = <1>{
    code = -32601,
    message = "Unhandled method completionItem/resolve",
    <metatable> = {
      __tostring = <function 1>
    }
  },
  error = <table 1>
}

```

As there is no `err` key on `v0.10.4`, on line [1123](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/18520ad6bbf7e6408b8449658326dc0c947c3507/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1123) the value becomes `resolved.result`, which is `nil`.

@echasnovski, shall I write a PR?

